# The frozen batch scripts are byte-locked: legacy/source/source-hashes.json records each file's exact
# size and SHA-256, and legacy/legacy-bundle.json is compiled from those exact bytes and checked against
# LegacyBundleIdentity.Sha256 at runtime.
#
# Git normalises line endings by default, which rewrites those bytes on checkout. The result is silent and
# serious: a fresh clone regenerates a bundle with a different hash, so nobody can reproduce the shipped
# one and the SHA-256 lock the README promises becomes unverifiable. Treat them as binary — they are data,
# not source anyone edits by hand.
legacy/source/** -text

# The compiled bundle and its ledger are generated artifacts and are compared byte-for-byte.
legacy/legacy-bundle.json -text
legacy/parity-manifest.json -text

# Screenshots used as acceptance evidence.
*.png binary
